-- R7 (#290): the planned nodes the farms move, re-planned (rural plan §7).
--
-- The farms' lanes and lots replace the old trails, and the plain's water
-- runs round the new roads, so the plan of the rural ring changes: its woods,
-- branches, outcrops and veins keep off the farms and the lanes. The woods
-- cover less of the ring with the farms in it, so a tree gets more tries to
-- find them (`node_spawn::WOODS_TRIES`), and D5's 955 trees are 954.
--
-- The wilds' land and water are the same past r4800, but their nodes are
-- planned after the rural ring's on the same spacing grid, by rejection
-- sampling: one rural node by the edge that turns down a wild spot changes
-- every draw after it in that stream. So the wilds' nodes move too, all but
-- the veins up in the ranges (#340). The city's and the suburb's nodes don't
-- move, and keep their rows, as do the 27 rural and wild ones the plan put
-- back exactly.
--
-- So this deletes the rows the plan no longer has, by id, and inserts the
-- new ones, as 20261125_001_rural_iron_veins.sql did for the veins. Nothing a
-- player owns is a node; a node half gathered starts over. No move migration
-- follows: the plan keeps off the water and the seeded grass, as moved by the
-- first set's 20261126_001_rural_farms.sql.
--
-- The rows come from the ignored test `print_node_replan`, and
-- `the_migration_writes_the_default_plan` checks the plan still matches.
--
-- deleted, 11278:
--   clay_bank in wilderness: 315
--   fallen_branches in rural: 573
--   fallen_branches in wilderness: 2364
--   iron_vein in rural: 76
--   old_growth in wilderness: 4727
--   reed_bed in wilderness: 473
--   rock_outcrop in rural: 229
--   rock_outcrop in wilderness: 1570
--   tree in rural: 951
